<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14068" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dĭŏnȳsus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διόνυσος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Greek name of Bacchus</i> (not in the
			Aug. poets), <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 3, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">23</span></i>; Att.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 6, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Stich. 5, 2, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr.
			30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dĭŏnȳsĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to Bacchus;</i>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dĭŏ-nȳsia</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διονύσια, τά</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερά</span>), <i>the festival of
				Bacchus</i>, in Greece celebrated every three years (Lat.
			Bacchanalia), <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 5, 2, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Cist.
				1, 1, 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 3, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ps. 1,
				1, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Heaut. 1, 1, 110</span></i> Don.;
					<i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 4,
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dĭŏnȳsĭas</span></b> ,
				ădis, f., <i>a
				precious stone, of a black color</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				10, 57, § 157</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dĭŏnȳsĭăcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>relating to Bacchus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ludi, i. q. Liberalia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ecl. de Feriis Rom. 29</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
